    <summary>Cleans damage from scanned prints, reconstructs faces and colorizes monochrome images offline, a local photo restoration software with batch mode and an 8x enlarger.</summary>
    <description>SoftOrbits Photo Retoucher is photo restoration software for Windows that cleans and repairs scanned old photographs on the local machine. The package is meant for libraries, local history archives and photo studios where several digitizing stations process donated or customer prints without sending them to an online service.

![Photo Retoucher screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ret/ret-v1-main.png)

## Before the first run

On first launch the program asks to download its AI models. Approve it on each workstation and let the download complete before handing the PC to staff. A CUDA-capable graphics card speeds things up, and machines without one run the same functions on the processor.

The same install also serves as photo retouching software for newer pictures, with manual brightness, contrast and saturation controls and an AI enlarger that scales small scans up to 8x before they go to print.

## How to use it

1. Load a scan in TIFF, PNG, JPEG or a RAW format.
2. Start the AI restoration with one click. It retouches faces and repairs blur, grain and surface damage.
3. Decide whether to colorize the image or leave it monochrome, then correct single colors manually if the AI picked the wrong shade.
4. Erase handwritten dates, stamps or stray objects with the Object Remover.
5. For a full box of prints, set up batch mode with only the steps you need and process them in one run.

&gt; Trial note: the free trial lets staff run every restoration step and inspect the output, but the unregistered version cannot save images. A license unlocks saving.

![Photo Retoucher screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ret/ret-v1-ai.png)

## Who it is for

- Archives and libraries digitizing donated photo collections.
- Photo studios offering repair of customer prints.
- Genealogy volunteers preparing portraits for family trees.
- Anyone who wants to remove scratches from photos without retouching each one by hand.

![Photo Retoucher screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/ret/ret-v1-result.png)

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of Photo Retoucher, commercial photo restoration software by SoftOrbits. Full use, including saving restored images, requires a paid license. Plans, including a business license: [old photo restoration software](https://www.softorbits.net/old-photo-restoration-software/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package).

[SoftOrbits Photo Retoucher on Windows Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9MWTL7ZFKS0V)

## FAQ

### What is the right way to restore old photos?

Start from the sharpest scan you can make, because a detailed scan gives the AI more to work with. Run the automatic repair first and use the manual tools only for what is left.

### How much does it cost to restore an old photo?

With this photo restoration software there is no fee per picture, since one license covers every photo you process. The trial is free to evaluate, and current prices are on the product site.

### Where can I get my old photos restored?

You can do old photo restoration yourself at home or at work with a scanner and this program, which keeps the prints and the files in your hands. For a large collection, batch mode handles a whole folder.
